Let f : [0, 3] → R be defined by f(x) = min{x – [x], 1 + [x] – x}
Where [x] is the greatest integer less than or equal to x.
Let P denote the set containing all x ∈ [0, 3] where f is discontinuous, and Q denote the set containing all x ∈ (0, 3) where f is not differentiable. Then the sum of number of elements in P and Q is equal to________.
